# ===========================================================================
#  apps.reg  -  starpOS application registry
# ===========================================================================
#  Every program the OS knows about. bootcore.bat auto-runs every .bat in
#  the system folder at boot, so this file is the human-readable index of
#  what those files actually are.
#
#  NOTE: this file is the INDEX. The desktop menu is a different file,
#  menu.cfg. Add an app to menu.cfg to make it appear on the desktop, and
#  add it here so you can still remember what it was in six months.
#
#  FORMAT:  slot|name|file|type|description
#
#     slot  = desktop menu number, or - if the app is not on the menu
#     type  = core     : part of the boot chain, do not launch by hand
#             app      : normal program the user can open
#             tool     : utility / diagnostic
#             lib      : support file, not launchable
# ===========================================================================

# --- Boot chain (do not launch these directly) ------------------------------
-|Boot Loader|boot.bat|core|Hardware check, splash screen, hands off to the kernel
-|Kernel Core|bootcore.bat|core|Sets OS variables, builds folders, scans and runs startup scripts
-|Desktop Shell|startup.bat|core|The desktop. v2.0, menu driven from menu.cfg
-|Desktop Shell v2|startup2.bat|core|Older desktop with the login portal
-|Data Engine|data\data.bat|core|Creates the data, debug, builds and resources folders
-|Update Stub|updates.bat|core|Empty placeholder the kernel skips on purpose

# --- Desktop applications (slots come from menu.cfg) ------------------------
1|File Explorer|startup.bat|app|Browse folders, go up with .., launch a file by name
2|Notepad|startup.bat|app|Multi line notes saved into data\notes
3|My Notes|startup.bat|app|List and read back everything you have written
4|System Info|startup.bat|app|The starpOS identity block, read from starpos.cfg
5|Real Machine Specs|sysinfo.ps1|app|Actual CPU, memory, disks, uptime and graphics
6|Log Viewer|logview.ps1|app|Reads the three log streams, colours them by tag
7|Task Manager|startup.bat|app|Live list of running processes
8|Search Files|startup.bat|app|Finds files by name anywhere under the starpOS root
9|Calculator|calc.ps1|app|Arithmetic with history and an ans key
10|Clock|startup.bat|app|Full screen clock, ticks once a second, Q to leave
11|Command Prompt|startup.bat|app|A real cmd shell, type exit to return
12|Settings|startup.bat|app|Themes, voice switch, session name, saves to starpos.cfg
13|AI Assistant|ai.bat|app|Kohaku pattern board, 33 call signs, learns new answers
13|AI Assistant (native)|ai.exe|app|The same assistant with a real window. Built from ai.cs
14|Voice Control|voice.ps1|app|Speech recognition driven by voice.cmds
15|Movie Theater|movies.bat|app|Scans the system folder for .mkv files and plays them
16|USB Devices|usb.bat|app|Scan, mount and eject external drives
18|Camera|camera app\camera.ps1|app|Takes real webcam photos into camera app\photos, with a gallery
H|Help|startup.bat|app|Prints help.txt
A|About starpOS|startup.bat|app|Logo and version.txt
X|Shut Down|startup.bat|app|Closes starpOS

# --- Other versions kept around ---------------------------------------------
-|AI Assistant v2|aiv2.bat|app|Speech engine v3.6
-|AI Assistant v3|aiv3.bat|app|Speech engine v4.0
-|Voice Control (batch)|Voice.bat|app|Original batch voice listener
-|Voice Control (native)|Voice.exe|app|Compiled from Voice.cs
-|Voice Control v2|voise2.bat|app|Voice input via a pop-up text box
-|Movie Theater v2|movies2.bat|app|Movie hub, second revision

# --- Developer mode (hidden until unlocked with D on the desktop) -----------
D|Developer Mode|startup.bat|app|The gate. Asks for DEV_PASS, then opens the dev menu
C|Dev Console|startup.bat|app|Runs any command you type, nothing filtered
S|System Scan|scan.ps1|tool|Deep read-only check of every file and every batch jump
R|Repair Errors|repair.ps1|tool|Finds known faults and fixes them, backing up first
L|Edit Logs|logedit.ps1|tool|View, search, trim, delete and wipe log streams
N|New App|mkapp.ps1|tool|Writes a working app from a template and adds it to the menu
I|Install App|install.ps1|tool|Registers programs, folders, websites and winget packages

# --- Tools ------------------------------------------------------------------
-|System Info Reporter|sysinfo.ps1|tool|Real machine specifications
-|Log Viewer|logview.ps1|tool|Also runs alone with -Stream, -Tail, -Filter, -Clear
-|Calculator|calc.ps1|tool|Also runs alone with -Expression "2+2"
-|Config Writer|setcfg.ps1|tool|Saves a setting back into starpos.cfg so it sticks
-|Code Debugger|..\debug\codedebuger.bat|tool|Checks whether each log stream is alive

# --- Voice system -----------------------------------------------------------
-|Voice Engine|voice.ps1|app|Listens on the mic, falls back to typing
-|Voice Commands|voice.cmds|lib|Every phrase the engine listens for
-|Voice Bank|voicebank.txt|lib|Every line starpOS speaks, looked up by ID
-|Speech Engine|speak.vbs|lib|Speaks one line, call it instead of writing temp VBS
-|Input Gateway|listen.vbs|lib|Pop-up input box, prints the answer for batch to catch

# --- Support files ----------------------------------------------------------
-|Call Signs|places.cfg|lib|The two letter codes the AI board is built from
-|System Config|starpos.cfg|lib|Master settings file
-|Desktop Menu|menu.cfg|lib|What appears on the desktop and what each item runs
-|Account Registry|users.db|lib|Usernames, passwords and roles
-|Boot Banner|logo.txt|lib|ASCII logo, print it with: type logo.txt
-|Message Of The Day|motd.txt|lib|Desktop welcome text
-|Help Text|help.txt|lib|In-OS help screen
-|Error Codes|errors.txt|lib|Every STARP error number and what it means
-|Version Info|version.txt|lib|Build number and change history
-|Manual|MANUAL.txt|lib|How the system files fit together
.com|youtube|start "" "https://www.youtube.com"|app|Opens https://www.youtube.com
